@page "/knowledge-base"
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Knowledge base for support teams";
    ViewData["Description"] = "How a problem was fixed, written from the ticket, filed in general or per client, searchable, with pictures and every version kept.";
}
<section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
        <h1>A knowledge base your whole team uses</h1>
        <p class="lede">The second time a problem comes in, the answer should already be written down. Here it is written from the ticket that
            solved it the first time — and found by anybody, from the console or the portal.</p>
        <div class="next-links"><partial name="_SiteCta" /></div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="facts">
            <div class="card fact"><h3>From the ticket</h3><p>When a job's work is recorded as done, <em>Add to knowledge base</em> opens a draft with what was done already in it. Edit it, save it.</p></div>
            <div class="card fact"><h3>General, or per client</h3><p>How to set up a printer belongs to everybody; how this client's server is set up belongs to them. A client's tickets and computers show their articles.</p></div>
            <div class="card fact"><h3>Folders and search</h3><p>Folders inside folders, and a search from wherever you are. Pictures pasted straight in, and buttons that open a link.</p></div>
            <div class="card fact"><h3>Nothing lost</h3><p>Everybody can edit, every save is kept and can be put back, and two people editing at once never overwrite each other. A password typed into an article is pointed out.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="next-links"><a class="btn" href="/ticketing">Ticketing</a> <a class="btn" href="/features">All features</a></div>
    </div>
</section>
